; $.SCREEN: &2800 bytes at sector &03E. The loading picture - a space
; station, planets and the "pipeline" logo over the Superior Software and
; Acornsoft logos - as a MODE 5 screen: the whole of screen memory from &5800
; to &7FFF, saved as it stood (docs/img/loading-screen.png, or render it with
; `tools/beebscreen.py 5 data/screen.bin OUT.png --palette 0,1,3,5`).
;
; MENU *LOADs it straight into screen memory as soon as its setup is done
; (line 250: MODE 5, cursor off, VDU 19,3,5 to make colour 3 magenta), so
; the palette is black, red, yellow, magenta; it stays up for ten seconds or
; until a key (INKEY(1000)). *LOAD runs nothing, so the catalogued exec
; address is unused.
;
; Layout is the MOS's for MODE 5: 32 character rows of 320 bytes, each row
; 40 blocks of 8 bytes (a block is 4 pixels wide, so a MODE 5 character is
; two), one byte per pixel line of the block; a byte is 4 pixels, pixel p's
; colour taking bit 7-p as its high bit and bit 3-p as its low. The picture
; fills the top 27 character rows; the last five are blank.

INCLUDE "osconst.6502inc"

SECTION screen, filename="SCREEN", org=MODE5_SCREEN, load=&5800, exec=&5800
.loading_screen
{
.picture
    INCBIN "../data/screen.bin"
    ASSERT P% = MODE5_SCREEN + 27 * MODE5_ROW_BYTES
.blank_rows
    SKIPTO SCREEN_MEMORY_END
}
ENDSECTION
